<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tulagi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tulagi is a small island in the Nggela group of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> Islands, off the south coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> Island. It was the capital of the British Solomon Islands <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> from 1896 until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, when the Japanese occupied it in May 1942 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> marines retook it in August 1942. The capital was later moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honiara">Honiara</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tulagi.jpg" alt="Tulagi" width="320" height="272" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kelisi at English Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NggelaSolomons.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
